[stderr] +
[stderr] +## First-release completeness and target parity
[stderr] +
[stderr] +P0 completes J1–J4 without G01–G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Capability | Responsive public web | PWA | Intentional difference |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |
[stderr] +| Input/responsive UI | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; phone/tablet/desktop. | Same browser-supported model/layouts. | Capability may limit gamepad; alternate input remains. |
[stderr] +| Offline | Play after required assets cache; local campaign needs no connection. | Same. | PWA adds install/app-shell cache state. |
[stderr] +| Update safety | Saves separate from assets. | Same. | PWA stages/activates cache visibly without save mutation. |
[stderr] +| Account/commerce/connected services | Not P0. | Not P0. | None until approval. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Decisions carried forward
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.
