[stderr] 64:## Domain chapters
[stderr] 66:### Game shell, session, and navigation
[stderr] 68:**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.
[stderr] 70:### Exploration and scenes
[stderr] 72:**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.
[stderr] 74:### Narrative, dialogue, and ending
[stderr] 76:**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible → presented → choice/advance → recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.
[stderr] 78:### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards
[stderr] 80:**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted → prompted → completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.
[stderr] 82:### Party combat and balance
[stderr] 84:**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.
[stderr] 86:### Inventory and equipment
[stderr] 88:**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.
[stderr] 90:### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle
[stderr] 92:**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.
[stderr] 94:### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation
[stderr] 96:**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load → edit → apply → persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.
[stderr] 98:### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery
[stderr] 102:### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations
[stderr] 104:**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages → validates → activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.
[stderr] 106:### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary
[stderr] 108:**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.
