[stderr] +# 02 — Feature model and release slices
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md), [normalized brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md), and [source brief](../INITIAL.md). This model preserves unresolved decisions rather than selecting services or technology.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Product, personas, and outcomes
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The first release is an original, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG: explore one town and one dungeon, advance a short quest chain through turn-based combat and rewards, save/resume, and reach a short ending. Responsive web and installable PWA deliver the same shared game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Persona | Job to be done | First useful outcome | Needs |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |
[stderr] +| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |
[stderr] +| Access-needs player | Play the same campaign with preferred input and reading settings. | Complete onboarding with usable controls and understandable feedback. | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; text, captions, visual settings, responsive UI. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Journey | Happy path and outcome | Relevant alternate paths |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| J1 First session | Start → onboarding → town objective → tutorial encounter → win/reward → confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |
[stderr] +| J2 Campaign | Load/new → town dialogue/quest → dungeon/encounters → rewards/inventory → quest completion → ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |
[stderr] +| J3 Resume/recovery | Open → select confirmed save → resume → pause/save → return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |
[stderr] +| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA → set input/settings → play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Every P0 feature maps to J1–J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Vocabulary, entities, and lifecycles
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Term/entity | Meaning, lifecycle, and rules |
[stderr] +| --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Campaign | Authored town-to-dungeon-to-ending progression. Definitions are content-owned; player completion is progression-owned. |
[stderr] +| Player profile | Local preferences and save index. An account is not assumed. |
[stderr] +| Save slot/snapshot | Named, versioned confirmed serialization: absent → new → checkpointed/confirmed → loaded → superseded or deletion-requested → deleted. Validate before session creation; failed migration/corruption leaves prior artifact untouched. Delete requires confirmation and affects only the selected slot. |
[stderr] +| Session | Runtime state derived from a valid snapshot; never the only durable progress record. Pause does not imply save. |
[stderr] +| Scene/trigger | Authored town/dungeon, collision, interactive object, exit, or encounter trigger: unavailable/idle → eligible → active → resolved/disabled. Broken destination/content is recoverable, never a soft-lock. |
[stderr] +| Quest/objective | Authored objective graph: unavailable → available → active → completed or failed → reward granted. Prerequisites and completion/reward are explicit and idempotent. |
[stderr] +| Encounter/combatant | Bounded turn-based event: armed → initiated → legal turn cycle → resolved (victory/defeat/authorised escape) → rewards/checkpoint eligible. Invalid actor/action/target changes no state or turn. |
[stderr] +| Item/inventory | Definition and stack: defined → granted → held → used/equipped/consumed or removed. Quantity is never negative; eligibility is validated. Any capacity policy must retain recoverable rewards. |
[stderr] +| Content package | Original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, art/audio and locale keys: drafted → reviewed → validated → packaged → cached/active → retired. Partial/incompatible package retains last known-good content. |
[stderr] +| Diagnostic record | detected → minimised/consent-gated → queued/sent → expired/deleted. It never blocks play or save; provider, retention, consent and deletion are open decisions. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## System relationship map
[stderr] +
[stderr] +```text
[stderr] +Authoring/validation ─packages─> Content (scenes, dialogue, quests, items,
[stderr] +                                encounters, localisation, art/audio)
[stderr] +                                      │                    │
[stderr] +Input + rendering + accessibility ─> Exploration ─interacts─> Narrative/quests
[stderr] +        │                              │                         │
[stderr] +        │                              └─starts─> Combat ─> Rewards/inventory
[stderr] +        └────settings apply to all player UI──────────────────────┘
[stderr] +                                                            │
[stderr] +                          Progression <──completion/reward──┘
[stderr] +                               │
[stderr] +Shell/session <──loads── Save/checkpoint <──serialises── shared game state
[stderr] +     │                         │                                   │
[stderr] +     ├─PWA cache/update────────┴─must never mutate────────────────┘
[stderr] +     └─error boundary/diagnostics ──> player recovery/support triage
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Release and quality validate every edge. Privacy/security constrain diagnostics
[stderr] +and any approved connected boundary. Account/sync, multiplayer, live operations,
[stderr] +and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.
[stderr] +```
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Domain chapters
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Game shell, session, and navigation
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Exploration and scenes
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Narrative, dialogue, and ending
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible → presented → choice/advance → recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted → prompted → completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Party combat and balance
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Inventory and equipment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load → edit → apply → persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** source assets and gameplay definitions, validation report, versioned package: draft → reviewed → validated → packaged → active/retired. **Rules/outcomes:** delivers original warm hand-painted, readable content for the complete P0 campaign. Validation checks required strings, links, exits, encounters, IDs, and asset availability; invalid packages cannot activate. **Inputs/dependencies:** feeds gameplay/presentation and release. **P0 boundary:** no copied assets/content, UGC/mod loading, or seasonal cadence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages → validates → activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Prioritised feature catalogue
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Priority/feature | Outcome/journey | Slice | Dependencies |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| P0 F01 Shell/new/resume | Safely begin or return (J1/J3). | New, load, pause, recovery navigation. | Saves, content, rendering. |
[stderr] +| P0 F02 Exploration | Progress campaign (J1/J2). | One town, one dungeon, interactions. | Content, input, quests, combat. |
[stderr] +| P0 F03 Narrative/ending | Understand and finish story (J2). | Original dialogue and short ending. | Content, locale, progression. |
[stderr] +| P0 F04 Quests/onboarding | Learn and know next goal (J1/J2). | Tutorial, bounded quest chain/rewards. | Narrative, combat, saves. |
[stderr] +| P0 F05 Turn combat | Complete encounters (J1/J2). | Authored combat and defeat recovery. | Content, progression, inventory. |
[stderr] +| P0 F06 Inventory/rewards | Understand/use rewards (J2). | Inspect, grant, legal use/equip. | Content, combat, saves. |
[stderr] +| P0 F07 Persistence | Resume without silent loss (J1/J3). | Local saves, checkpoints, validation, recovery, deletion. | Storage, content version. |
[stderr] +| P0 F08 Accessible responsive input/settings | Play/read with preferences (J1/J4). | Responsive UI, inputs, text/captions/visual settings. | UI domains, platform APIs. |
[stderr] +| P0 F09 Original content delivery | Coherent original campaign (J1/J2). | Validated original packages/assets. | Authoring, release. |
[stderr] +| P0 F10 PWA/offline/update | Install and continue safely (J3/J4). | Installability, offline assets/saves, safe cache update. | Persistence, release. |
[stderr] +| P0 F11 Error recovery/quality | Recover from failure (J3/J4). | Player recovery UI, approved minimal diagnostics, target testing. | Shell, privacy decisions. |
[stderr] +| Gate G01 Account/remote state | Optional continuity only if approved. | Not P0; local profile/save only. | Privacy/security, backend. |
[stderr] +| Gate G02 Multiplayer/safety/live ops | Social play only if re-authorised. | Not P0; single player only. | Identity, legal, operations. |
[stderr] +| Gate G03 Purchases/entitlements | Commerce only if re-authorised. | Not P0; no paid content. | Identity, legal, operations. |
[stderr] +| Deferred D01 Events, UGC, advanced analytics/monetisation | Extend later. | Explicitly deferred. | Content pipeline, connected policy. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## First-release completeness and target parity
[stderr] +
[stderr] +P0 completes J1–J4 without G01–G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Capability | Responsive public web | PWA | Intentional difference |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |
[stderr] +| Input/responsive UI | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; phone/tablet/desktop. | Same browser-supported model/layouts. | Capability may limit gamepad; alternate input remains. |
[stderr] +| Offline | Play after required assets cache; local campaign needs no connection. | Same. | PWA adds install/app-shell cache state. |
[stderr] +| Update safety | Saves separate from assets. | Same. | PWA stages/activates cache visibly without save mutation. |
[stderr] +| Account/commerce/connected services | Not P0. | Not P0. | None until approval. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Decisions carried forward
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.
[stderr] 
