ed game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.\n11:| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |\n12:| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |\n17:| J1 First session | Start \u2192 onboarding \u2192 town objective \u2192 tutorial encounter \u2192 win/reward \u2192 confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |\n18:| J2 Campaign | Load/new \u2192 town dialogue/quest \u2192 dungeon/encounters \u2192 rewards/inventory \u2192 quest completion \u2192 ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |\n19:| J3 Resume/recovery | Open \u2192 select confirmed save \u2192 resume \u2192 pause/save \u2192 return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |\n20:| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA \u2192 set input/settings \u2192 play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |\n22:Every P0 feature maps to J1\u2013J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.\n24:## Vocabulary, entities, and lifecycles\n30:| Save slot/snapshot | Named, versioned confirmed serialization: absent \u2192 new \u2192 checkpointed/confirmed \u2192 loaded \u2192 superseded or deletion-requested \u2192 deleted. Validate before session creation; failed migration/corruption leaves prior artifact untouched. Delete requires confirmation and affects only the selected slot. |\n37:| Diagnostic record | detected \u2192 minimised/consent-gated \u2192 queued/sent \u2192 expired/deleted. It never blocks play or save; provider, retention, consent and deletion are open decisions. |\n39:## System relationship map\n55:     \u2514\u2500error boundary/diagnostics \u2500\u2500> player recovery/support triage\n59:and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.\n62:**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.\n64:## Domain chapters\n66:### Game shell, session, and navigation\n68:**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.\n70:### Exploration and scenes\n72:**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.\n74:### Narrative, dialogue, and ending\n76:**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible \u2192 presented \u2192 choice/advance \u2192 recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.\n78:### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards\n80:**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted \u2192 prompted \u2192 completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.\n82:### Party combat and balance\n84:**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.\n86:### Inventory and equipment\n88:**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.\n90:### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle\n92:**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.\n94:### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation\n96:**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load \u2192 edit \u2192 apply \u2192 persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.\n98:### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery\n102:### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations\n104:**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages \u2192 validates \u2192 activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.\n106:### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary\n108:**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.\n110:## Prioritised feature catalogue\n114:| P0 F01 Shell/new/resume | Safely begin or return (J1/J3). | New, load, pause, recovery navigation. | Saves, content, rendering. |\n115:| P0 F02 Exploration | Progress campaign (J1/J2). | One town, one dungeon, interactions. | Content, input, quests, combat. |\n116:| P0 F03 Narrative/ending | Understand and finish story (J2). | Original dialogue and short ending. | Content, locale, progression. |\n117:| P0 F04 Quests/onboarding | Learn and know next goal (J1/J2). | Tutorial, bounded quest chain/rewards. | Narrative, combat, saves. |\n118:| P0 F05 Turn combat | Complete encounters (J1/J2). | Authored combat and defeat recovery. | Content, progression, inventory. |\n119:| P0 F06 Inventory/rewards | Understand/use rewards (J2). | Inspect, grant, legal use/equip. | Content, combat, saves. |\n120:| P0 F07 Persistence | Resume without silent loss (J1/J3). | Local saves, checkpoints, validation, recovery, deletion. | Storage, content version. |\n121:| P0 F08 Accessible responsive input/settings | Play/read with preferences (J1/J4). | Responsive UI, inputs, text/captions/visual settings. | UI domains, platform APIs. |\n122:| P0 F09 Original content delivery | Coherent original campaign (J1/J2). | Validated original packages/assets. | Authoring, release. |\n123:| P0 F10 PWA/offline/update | Install and continue safely (J3/J4). | Installability, offline assets/saves, safe cache update. | Persistence, release. |\n124:| P0 F11 Error recovery/quality | Recover from failure (J3/J4). | Player recovery UI, approved minimal diagnostics, target testing. | Shell, privacy decisions. |\n125:| Gate G01 Account/remote state | Optional continuity only if approved. | Not P0; local profile/save only. | Privacy/security, backend. |\n126:| Gate G02 Multiplayer/safety/live ops | Social play only if re-authorised. | Not P0; single player only. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n127:| Gate G03 Purchases/entitlements | Commerce only if re-authorised. | Not P0; no paid content. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n128:| Deferred D01 Events, UGC, advanced analytics/monetisation | Extend later. | Explicitly deferred. | Content pipeline, connected policy. |\n130:## First-release completeness and target parity\n132:P0 completes J1\u2013J4 without G01\u2013G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.\n136:| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |\n142:## Decisions carried forward\n144:Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\n\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..020702b2a410cbe74dcade94a047bd014bf63347\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+# 02 \u2014 Feature model and release slices\n+\n+**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md), [normalized brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md), and [source brief](../INITIAL.md). This model preserves unresolved decisions rather than selecting services or technology.\n+\n+## Product, personas, and outcomes\n+\n+The first release is an original, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG: explore one town and one dungeon, advance a short quest chain through turn-based combat and rewards, save/resume, and reach a short ending. Responsive web and installable PWA deliver the same shared game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.\n+\n+| Persona | Job to be done | First useful outcome | Needs |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |\n+| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |\n+| Access-needs player | Play the same campaign with preferred input and reading settings. | Complete onboarding with usable controls and understandable feedback. | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; text, captions, visual settings, responsive UI. |\n+\n+| Journey | Happy path and outcome | Relevant alternate paths |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| J1 First session | Start \u2192 onboarding \u2192 town objective \u2192 tutorial encounter \u2192 win/reward \u2192 confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |\n+| J2 Campaign | Load/new \u2192 town dialogue/quest \u2192 dungeon/encounters \u2192 rewards/inventory \u2192 quest completion \u2192 ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |\n+| J3 Resume/recovery | Open \u2192 select confirmed save \u2192 resume \u2192 pause/save \u2192 return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |\n+| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA \u2192 set input/settings \u2192 play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |\n+\n+Every P0 feature maps to J1\u2013J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.\n+\n+## Vocabulary, entities, and lifecycles\n+\n+| Term/entity | Meaning, lifecycle, and rules |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Campaign | Authored town-to-dungeon-to-ending progression. Definitions are content-owned; player completion is progression-owned. |\n+| Player profile | Local preferences and save index. An account is not assumed. |\n+| Save slot/snapshot | Named, versioned confirmed serialization: absent \u2192 new \u2192 checkpointed/confirmed \u2192 loaded \u2192 superseded or deletion-requested \u2192 deleted. Validate before session creation; failed migration/corruption leaves prior artifact untouched. Delete requires confirmation and affects only the selected slot. |\n+| Session | Runtime state derived from a valid snapshot; never the only durable progress record. Pause does not imply save. |\n+| Scene/trigger | Authored town/dungeon, collision, interactive object, exit, or encounter trigger: unavailable/idle \u2192 eligible \u2192 active \u2192 resolved/disabled. Broken destination/content is recoverable, never a soft-lock. |\n+| Quest/objective | Authored objective graph: unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 active \u2192 completed or failed \u2192 reward granted. Prerequisites and completion/reward are explicit and idempotent. |\n+| Encounter/combatant | Bounded turn-based event: armed \u2192 initiated \u2192 legal turn cycle \u2192 resolved (victory/defeat/authorised escape) \u2192 rewards/checkpoint eligible. Invalid actor/action/target changes no state or turn. |\n+| Item/inventory | Definition and stack: defined \u2192 granted \u2192 held \u2192 used/equipped/consumed or removed. Quantity is never negative; eligibility is validated. Any capacity policy must retain recoverable rewards. |\n+| Content package | Original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, art/audio and locale keys: drafted \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 cached/active \u2192 retired. Partial/incompatible package retains last known-good content. |\n+| Diagnostic record | detected \u2192 minimised/consent-gated \u2192 queued/sent \u2192 expired/deleted. It never blocks play or save; provider, retention, consent and deletion are open decisions. |\n+\n+## System relationship map\n+\n+```text\n+Authoring/validation \u2500packages\u2500> Content (scenes, dialogue, quests, items,\n+                                encounters, localisation, art/audio)\n+                                      \u2502                    \u2502\n+Input + rendering + accessibility \u2500> Exploration \u2500interacts\u2500> Narrative/quests\n+        \u2502                              \u2502                         \u2502\n+        \u2502                              \u2514\u2500starts\u2500> Combat \u2500> Rewards/inventory\n+        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500settings apply to all player UI\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                                                            \u2502\n+                          Progression <\u2500\u2500completion/reward\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                               \u2502\n+Shell/session <\u2500\u2500loads\u2500\u2500 Save/checkpoint <\u2500\u2500serialises\u2500\u2500 shared game state\n+     \u2502                         \u2502                                   \u2502\n+     \u251c\u2500PWA cache/update\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500must never mutate\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+     \u2514\u2500error boundary/diagnostics \u2500\u2500> player recovery/support triage\n+\n+Release and quality validate every edge. Privacy/security constrain diagnostics\n+and any approved connected boundary. Account/sync, multiplayer, live operations,\n+and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.\n+```\n+\n+**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.\n+\n+## Domain chapters\n+\n+### Game shell, session, and navigation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.\n+\n+### Exploration and scenes\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.\n+\n+### Narrative, dialogue, and ending\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible \u2192 presented \u2192 choice/advance \u2192 recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.\n+\n+### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted \u2192 prompted \u2192 completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.\n+\n+### Party combat and balance\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.\n+\n+### Inventory and equipment\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.\n+\n+### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.\n+\n+### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load \u2192 edit \u2192 apply \u2192 persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.\n+\n+### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** source assets and gameplay definitions, validation report, versioned package: draft \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 active/retired. **Rules/outcomes:** delivers original warm hand-painted, readable content for the complete P0 campaign. Validation checks required strings, links, exits, encounters, IDs, and asset availability; invalid packages cannot activate. **Inputs/dependencies:** feeds gameplay/presentation and release. **P0 boundary:** no copied assets/content, UGC/mod loading, or seasonal cadence.\n+\n+### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages \u2192 validates \u2192 activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.\n+\n+### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.\n+\n+## Prioritised feature catalogue\n+\n+| Priority/feature | Outcome/journey | Slice | Dependencies |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| P0 F01 Shell/new/resume | Safely begin or return (J1/J3). | New, load, pause, recovery navigation. | Saves, content, rendering. |\n+| P0 F02 Exploration | Progress campaign (J1/J2). | One town, one dungeon, interactions. | Content, input, quests, combat. |\n+| P0 F03 Narrative/ending | Understand and finish story (J2). | Original dialogue and short ending. | Content, locale, progression. |\n+| P0 F04 Quests/onboarding | Learn and know next goal (J1/J2). | Tutorial, bounded quest chain/rewards. | Narrative, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F05 Turn combat | Complete encounters (J1/J2). | Authored combat and defeat recovery. | Content, progression, inventory. |\n+| P0 F06 Inventory/rewards | Understand/use rewards (J2). | Inspect, grant, legal use/equip. | Content, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F07 Persistence | Resume without silent loss (J1/J3). | Local saves, checkpoints, validation, recovery, deletion. | Storage, content version. |\n+| P0 F08 Accessible responsive input/settings | Play/read with preferences (J1/J4). | Responsive UI, inputs, text/captions/visual settings. | UI domains, platform APIs. |\n+| P0 F09 Original content delivery | Coherent original campaign (J1/J2). | Validated original packages/assets. | Authoring, release. |\n+| P0 F10 PWA/offline/update | Install and continue safely (J3/J4). | Installability, offline assets/saves, safe cache update. | Persistence, release. |\n+| P0 F11 Error recovery/quality | Recover from failure (J3/J4). | Player recovery UI, approved minimal diagnostics, target testing. | Shell, privacy decisions. |\n+| Gate G01 Account/remote state | Optional continuity only if approved. | Not P0; local profile/save only. | Privacy/security, backend. |\n+| Gate G02 Multiplayer/safety/live ops | Social play only if re-authorised. | Not P0; single player only. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Gate G03 Purchases/entitlements | Commerce only if re-authorised. | Not P0; no paid content. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Deferred D01 Events, UGC, advanced analytics/monetisation | Extend later. | Explicitly deferred. | Content pipeline, connected policy. |\n+\n+## First-release completeness and target parity\n+\n+P0 completes J1\u2013J4 without G01\u2013G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.\n+\n+| Capability | Responsive public web | PWA | Intentional difference |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |\n+| Input/responsive UI | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; phone/tablet/desktop. | Same browser-supported model/layouts. | Capability may limit gamepad; alternate input remains. |\n+| Offline | Play after required assets cache; local campaign needs no connection. | Same. | PWA adds install/app-shell cache state. |\n+| Update safety | Saves separate from assets. | Same. | PWA stages/activates cache visibly without save mutation. |\n+| Account/commerce/connected services | Not P0. | Not P0. | None until approval. |\n+\n+## Decisions carried forward\n+\n+Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created the feature model with eleven accepted domain chapters, a cross-domain relationship/invariant map, complete offline release slice, and explicit gates for unresolved connected scope. Focused markdown checks pass.\",\"changed_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\"],\"test_result\":\"`git diff --check -- projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md` exited 0. A scoped `rg` content check confirmed required journeys, domain headings, recovery/offline/conflict/deletion coverage, release catalogue, and target-parity section.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Reviewed F001 discovery outputs and wrote the canonical F002 feature-model specification.\",\"adapter_log\":\"The requested codebase-memory architecture call was cancelled by the environment, so scoped repository file discovery was used for non-code Markdown sources.\",\"test_log\":\"Whitespace check passed; scoped content-presence check passed.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: this task creates a domain specification only.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Every feature maps to a user outcome and journey.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The J1\u2013J4 journey table and P0 feature catalogue explicitly map each P0 feature to player outcomes and journey IDs.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Normal, empty, invalid, permission-denied, offline, conflict, recovery, and deletion paths are specified where relevant.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"J1\u2013J4, entity lifecycles, persistence, presentation, PWA, and connected-boundary chapters define these paths, including storage denial, corrupt saves, unsupported input, offline cache misses, future sync conflict, and confirmed slot deletion.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The first release provides one complete useful journey without deferred dependencies.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The first-release completeness section establishes that P0 completes J1\u2013J4 as a local campaign without account, multiplayer, commerce, or live-service gates.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Cross-target capability parity and intentional target-specific differences are documented.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The target-parity table identifies shared core capabilities and PWA-specific installation/cache behavior plus browser capability fallbacks.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Each domain chapter defines its entities, rules, lifecycle, authoring inputs, dependencies, player/user outcomes, edge cases, and first-release boundary.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Eleven domain chapters cover shell, exploration, narrative, quests, combat, inventory, persistence, presentation, content tooling, platform/quality, and connected boundaries with the requested elements.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The relationship map identifies cross-domain invariants and lifecycle boundaries. For example, an RPG quest links narrative and save state; an IDE edit links language analysis, workspace indexing, and version control; an OS permission links identity, process, storage, and user settings.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The system relationship map and invariant paragraph connect authored content, exploration, narrative/quests, combat, rewards, progression, saves, PWA cache updates, and recovery; they define transactional completion/reward persistence and cache/save boundaries.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/INITIAL.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/README.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/README.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\"],\"summary\":\"Added the task-required canonical feature-model specification. Repository README files describe the factory rather than this project\u2019s feature model, so no README update was needed.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"Technical stack, support matrix/budgets, content quantities, localisation/audio detail, diagnostics policy, and all connected account/multiplayer/commerce decisions remain explicitly open as required by the source brief.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only domain modelling; no browser behavior or task-specific Playwright spec changed.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..020702b2a410cbe74dcade94a047bd014bf63347\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+# 02 \u2014 Feature model and release slices\n+\n+**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md), [normalized brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md), and [source brief](../INITIAL.md). This model preserves unresolved decisions rather than selecting services or technology.\n+\n+## Product, personas, and outcomes\n+\n+The first release is an original, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG: explore one town and one dungeon, advance a short quest chain through turn-based combat and rewards, save/resume, and reach a short ending. Responsive web and installable PWA deliver the same shared game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.\n+\n+| Persona | Job to be done | First useful outcome | Needs |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |\n+| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |\n+| Access-needs player | Play the same campaign with preferred input and reading settings. | Complete onboarding with usable controls and understandable feedback. | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; text, captions, visual settings, responsive UI. |\n+\n+| Journey | Happy path and outcome | Relevant alternate paths |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| J1 First session | Start \u2192 onboarding \u2192 town objective \u2192 tutorial encounter \u2192 win/reward \u2192 confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |\n+| J2 Campaign | Load/new \u2192 town dialogue/quest \u2192 dungeon/encounters \u2192 rewards/inventory \u2192 quest completion \u2192 ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |\n+| J3 Resume/recovery | Open \u2192 select confirmed save \u2192 resume \u2192 pause/save \u2192 return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |\n+| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA \u2192 set input/settings \u2192 play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |\n+\n+Every P0 feature maps to J1\u2013J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.\n+\n+## Vocabulary, entities, and lifecycles\n+\n+| Term/entity | Meaning, lifecycle, and rules |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Campaign | Authored town-to-dungeon-to-ending progression. Definitions are content-owned; player completion is progression-owned. |\n+| Player profile | Local preferences and save index. An account is not assumed. |\n+| Save slot/snapshot | Named, versioned confirmed serialization: absent \u2192 new \u2192 checkpointed/confirmed \u2192 loaded \u2192 superseded or deletion-requested \u2192 deleted. Validate before session creation; failed migration/corruption leaves prior artifact untouched. Delete requires confirmation and affects only the selected slot. |\n+| Session | Runtime state derived from a valid snapshot; never the only durable progress record. Pause does not imply save. |\n+| Scene/trigger | Authored town/dungeon, collision, interactive object, exit, or encounter trigger: unavailable/idle \u2192 eligible \u2192 active \u2192 resolved/disabled. Broken destination/content is recoverable, never a soft-lock. |\n+| Quest/objective | Authored objective graph: unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 active \u2192 completed or failed \u2192 reward granted. Prerequisites and completion/reward are explicit and idempotent. |\n+| Encounter/combatant | Bounded turn-based event: armed \u2192 initiated \u2192 legal turn cycle \u2192 resolved (victory/defeat/authorised escape) \u2192 rewards/checkpoint eligible. Invalid actor/action/target changes no state or turn. |\n+| Item/inventory | Definition and stack: defined \u2192 granted \u2192 held \u2192 used/equipped/consumed or removed. Quantity is never negative; eligibility is validated. Any capacity policy must retain recoverable rewards. |\n+| Content package | Original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, art/audio and locale keys: drafted \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 cached/active \u2192 retired. Partial/incompatible package retains last known-good content. |\n+| Diagnostic record | detected \u2192 minimised/consent-gated \u2192 queued/sent \u2192 expired/deleted. It never blocks play or save; provider, retention, consent and deletion are open decisions. |\n+\n+## System relationship map\n+\n+```text\n+Authoring/validation \u2500packages\u2500> Content (scenes, dialogue, quests, items,\n+                                encounters, localisation, art/audio)\n+                                      \u2502                    \u2502\n+Input + rendering + accessibility \u2500> Exploration \u2500interacts\u2500> Narrative/quests\n+        \u2502                              \u2502                         \u2502\n+        \u2502                              \u2514\u2500starts\u2500> Combat \u2500> Rewards/inventory\n+        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500settings apply to all player UI\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                                                            \u2502\n+                          Progression <\u2500\u2500completion/reward\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                               \u2502\n+Shell/session <\u2500\u2500loads\u2500\u2500 Save/checkpoint <\u2500\u2500serialises\u2500\u2500 shared game state\n+     \u2502                         \u2502                                   \u2502\n+     \u251c\u2500PWA cache/update\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500must never mutate\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+     \u2514\u2500error boundary/diagnostics \u2500\u2500> player recovery/support triage\n+\n+Release and quality validate every edge. Privacy/security constrain diagnostics\n+and any approved connected boundary. Account/sync, multiplayer, live operations,\n+and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.\n+```\n+\n+**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.\n+\n+## Domain chapters\n+\n+### Game shell, session, and navigation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.\n+\n+### Exploration and scenes\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.\n+\n+### Narrative, dialogue, and ending\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible \u2192 presented \u2192 choice/advance \u2192 recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.\n+\n+### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted \u2192 prompted \u2192 completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.\n+\n+### Party combat and balance\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.\n+\n+### Inventory and equipment\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.\n+\n+### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.\n+\n+### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load \u2192 edit \u2192 apply \u2192 persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.\n+\n+### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** source assets and gameplay definitions, validation report, versioned package: draft \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 active/retired. **Rules/outcomes:** delivers original warm hand-painted, readable content for the complete P0 campaign. Validation checks required strings, links, exits, encounters, IDs, and asset availability; invalid packages cannot activate. **Inputs/dependencies:** feeds gameplay/presentation and release. **P0 boundary:** no copied assets/content, UGC/mod loading, or seasonal cadence.\n+\n+### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages \u2192 validates \u2192 activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.\n+\n+### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.\n+\n+## Prioritised feature catalogue\n+\n+| Priority/feature | Outcome/journey | Slice | Dependencies |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| P0 F01 Shell/new/resume | Safely begin or return (J1/J3). | New, load, pause, recovery navigation. | Saves, content, rendering. |\n+| P0 F02 Exploration | Progress campaign (J1/J2). | One town, one dungeon, interactions. | Content, input, quests, combat. |\n+| P0 F03 Narrative/ending | Understand and finish story (J2). | Original dialogue and short ending. | Content, locale, progression. |\n+| P0 F04 Quests/onboarding | Learn and know next goal (J1/J2). | Tutorial, bounded quest chain/rewards. | Narrative, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F05 Turn combat | Complete encounters (J1/J2). | Authored combat and defeat recovery. | Content, progression, inventory. |\n+| P0 F06 Inventory/rewards | Understand/use rewards (J2). | Inspect, grant, legal use/equip. | Content, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F07 Persistence | Resume without silent loss (J1/J3). | Local saves, checkpoints, validation, recovery, deletion. | Storage, content version. |\n+| P0 F08 Accessible responsive input/settings | Play/read with preferences (J1/J4). | Responsive UI, inputs, text/captions/visual settings. | UI domains, platform APIs. |\n+| P0 F09 Original content delivery | Coherent original campaign (J1/J2). | Validated original packages/assets. | Authoring, release. |\n+| P0 F10 PWA/offline/update | Install and continue safely (J3/J4). | Installability, offline assets/saves, safe cache update. | Persistence, release. |\n+| P0 F11 Error recovery/quality | Recover from failure (J3/J4). | Player recovery UI, approved minimal diagnostics, target testing. | Shell, privacy decisions. |\n+| Gate G01 Account/remote state | Optional continuity only if approved. | Not P0; local profile/save only. | Privacy/security, backend. |\n+| Gate G02 Multiplayer/safety/live ops | Social play only if re-authorised. | Not P0; single player only. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Gate G03 Purchases/entitlements | Commerce only if re-authorised. | Not P0; no paid content. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Deferred D01 Events, UGC, advanced analytics/monetisation | Extend later. | Explicitly deferred. | Content pipeline, connected policy. |\n+\n+## First-release completeness and target parity\n+\n+P0 completes J1\u2013J4 without G01\u2013G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.\n+\n+| Capability | Responsive public web | PWA | Intentional difference |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |\n+| Input/responsive UI | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; phone/tablet/desktop. | Same browser-supported model/layouts. | Capability may limit gamepad; alternate input remains. |\n+| Offline | Play after required assets cache; local campaign needs no connection. | Same. | PWA adds install/app-shell cache state. |\n+| Update safety | Saves separate from assets. | Same. | PWA stages/activates cache visibly without save mutation. |\n+| Account/commerce/connected services | Not P0. | Not P0. | None until approval. |\n+\n+## Decisions carried forward\n+\n+Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created the F002 feature-model specification with domain chapters, journeys, lifecycles, release slices, and target parity.\",\"changed_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\"],\"test_result\":\"`git diff --check -- projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md` passed (exit 0). A scoped `rg` presence check confirmed journeys, domain chapters, recovery/offline/conflict/deletion coverage, release catalogue, and target parity.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Reviewed F001 discovery outputs and wrote the canonical F002 feature-model specification.\",\"adapter_log\":\"The codebase-memory architecture call was cancelled by the environment; scoped repository discovery was used for the non-code Markdown sources.\",\"test_log\":\"Whitespace check passed; scoped content-presence check passed.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only domain modelling.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Every feature maps to a user outcome and journey.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The J1\u2013J4 journey table and P0 catalogue map each first-release feature to user outcomes and journey IDs.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Normal, empty, invalid, permission-denied, offline, conflict, recovery, and deletion paths are specified where relevant.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Journeys, lifecycles, persistence, presentation, PWA, and connected-boundary chapters cover these paths.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The first release provides one complete useful journey without deferred dependencies.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The completeness section defines a local campaign completing J1\u2013J4 without connected-service gates.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Cross-target capability parity and intentional target-specific differences are documented.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The target-parity table documents shared web/PWA core and intentional PWA installation/cache differences.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Each domain chapter defines its entities, rules, lifecycle, authoring inputs, dependencies, player/user outcomes, edge cases, and first-release boundary.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Eleven domain chapters cover all accepted discovery families with these elements.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The relationship map identifies cross-domain invariants and lifecycle boundaries. For example, an RPG quest links narrative and save state; an IDE edit links language analysis, workspace indexing, and version control; an OS permission links identity, process, storage, and user settings.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The system map and invariants link content, quests, combat, rewards, progression, saves, cache updates, and recovery boundaries.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/00-domain-discovery.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/INITIAL.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/README.md\",\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/README.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\"],\"summary\":\"Added the required canonical feature-model specification. Repository README files describe the factory and did not require project-specific changes.\"},\"known_limitations\":[\"Stack, support matrix/budgets, content quantities, localisation/audio details, diagnostics policy, and connected account/multiplayer/commerce decisions remain explicitly open per the source brief.\"],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only domain modelling; no browser behavior or Playwright specification changed.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..020702b2a410cbe74dcade94a047bd014bf63347\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+# 02 \u2014 Feature model and release slices\n+\n+**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md), [normalized brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md), and [source brief](../INITIAL.md). This model preserves unresolved decisions rather than selecting services or technology.\n+\n+## Product, personas, and outcomes\n+\n+The first release is an original, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG: explore one town and one dungeon, advance a short quest chain through turn-based combat and rewards, save/resume, and reach a short ending. Responsive web and installable PWA deliver the same shared game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.\n+\n+| Persona | Job to be done | First useful outcome | Needs |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |\n+| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |\n+| Access-needs player | Play the same campaign with preferred input and reading settings. | Complete onboarding with usable controls and understandable feedback. | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; text, captions, visual settings, responsive UI. |\n+\n+| Journey | Happy path and outcome | Relevant alternate paths |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| J1 First session | Start \u2192 onboarding \u2192 town objective \u2192 tutorial encounter \u2192 win/reward \u2192 confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |\n+| J2 Campaign | Load/new \u2192 town dialogue/quest \u2192 dungeon/encounters \u2192 rewards/inventory \u2192 quest completion \u2192 ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |\n+| J3 Resume/recovery | Open \u2192 select confirmed save \u2192 resume \u2192 pause/save \u2192 return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |\n+| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA \u2192 set input/settings \u2192 play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |\n+\n+Every P0 feature maps to J1\u2013J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.\n+\n+## Vocabulary, entities, and lifecycles\n+\n+| Term/entity | Meaning, lifecycle, and rules |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Campaign | Authored town-to-dungeon-to-ending progression. Definitions are content-owned; player completion is progression-owned. |\n+| Player profile | Local preferences and save index. An account is not assumed. |\n+| Save slot/snapshot | Named, versioned confirmed serialization: absent \u2192 new \u2192 checkpointed/confirmed \u2192 loaded \u2192 superseded or deletion-requested \u2192 deleted. Validate before session creation; failed migration/corruption leaves prior artifact untouched. Delete requires confirmation and affects only the selected slot. |\n+| Session | Runtime state derived from a valid snapshot; never the only durable progress record. Pause does not imply save. |\n+| Scene/trigger | Authored town/dungeon, collision, interactive object, exit, or encounter trigger: unavailable/idle \u2192 eligible \u2192 active \u2192 resolved/disabled. Broken destination/content is recoverable, never a soft-lock. |\n+| Quest/objective | Authored objective graph: unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 active \u2192 completed or failed \u2192 reward granted. Prerequisites and completion/reward are explicit and idempotent. |\n+| Encounter/combatant | Bounded turn-based event: armed \u2192 initiated \u2192 legal turn cycle \u2192 resolved (victory/defeat/authorised escape) \u2192 rewards/checkpoint eligible. Invalid actor/action/target changes no state or turn. |\n+| Item/inventory | Definition and stack: defined \u2192 granted \u2192 held \u2192 used/equipped/consumed or removed. Quantity is never negative; eligibility is validated. Any capacity policy must retain recoverable rewards. |\n+| Content package | Original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, art/audio and locale keys: drafted \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 cached/active \u2192 retired. Partial/incompatible package retains last known-good content. |\n+| Diagnostic record | detected \u2192 minimised/consent-gated \u2192 queued/sent \u2192 expired/deleted. It never blocks play or save; provider, retention, consent and deletion are open decisions. |\n+\n+## System relationship map\n+\n+```text\n+Authoring/validation \u2500packages\u2500> Content (scenes, dialogue, quests, items,\n+                                encounters, localisation, art/audio)\n+                                      \u2502                    \u2502\n+Input + rendering + accessibility \u2500> Exploration \u2500interacts\u2500> Narrative/quests\n+        \u2502                              \u2502                         \u2502\n+        \u2502                              \u2514\u2500starts\u2500> Combat \u2500> Rewards/inventory\n+        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500settings apply to all player UI\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                                                            \u2502\n+                          Progression <\u2500\u2500completion/reward\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+                               \u2502\n+Shell/session <\u2500\u2500loads\u2500\u2500 Save/checkpoint <\u2500\u2500serialises\u2500\u2500 shared game state\n+     \u2502                         \u2502                                   \u2502\n+     \u251c\u2500PWA cache/update\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500must never mutate\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n+     \u2514\u2500error boundary/diagnostics \u2500\u2500> player recovery/support triage\n+\n+Release and quality validate every edge. Privacy/security constrain diagnostics\n+and any approved connected boundary. Account/sync, multiplayer, live operations,\n+and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.\n+```\n+\n+**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.\n+\n+## Domain chapters\n+\n+### Game shell, session, and navigation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** boot, title/menu, session, pause, recovery modal, and scene transition. Boot validates active content and save index; selecting a valid snapshot creates a session; quit ends runtime only. **Rules/outcomes:** new game, load/resume, settings, pause, permitted save, and return-to-menu make J1/J3 safe. No-save is normal; invalid slot returns recovery UI; reload/crash returns through validation. **Inputs/dependencies:** persistence, content version, rendering/input, recovery UI. **P0 boundary:** excludes social/home feed and login.\n+\n+### Exploration and scenes\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** scene definitions, location, collision, interactions, exits, triggers. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J2 traverse exactly one town and one dungeon, find objectives, and transition to dialogue/combat. Collision applies; locked routes explain prerequisites; empty/broken scene content triggers recovery rather than soft-lock. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored maps/collision/exits and validation; input/rendering, quests, combat, saves. **P0 boundary:** no extra, procedural, or user-created regions.\n+\n+### Narrative, dialogue, and ending\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** character, dialogue node/choice, locale key, narrative flag, ending: eligible \u2192 presented \u2192 choice/advance \u2192 recorded outcome. **Rules/outcomes:** original readable dialogue explains J2 and a short ending concludes it. Empty optional dialogue has neutral fallback; missing required text/localisation blocks delivery; effects are explicit and persisted. **Inputs/dependencies:** original writing, localisation, feedback, quest flags, saves. **P0 boundary:** compact campaign only; no copied reference material or expansion.\n+\n+### Quests, progression, onboarding, and rewards\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** quest graph, objective, prerequisite, tutorial step, flag, reward grant; onboarding unstarted \u2192 prompted \u2192 completed/resumed. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 teaches first combat and saving; J2 exposes an actionable objective. Prerequisites block invalid skips; repeat completion cannot duplicate reward; invalid data restores prior confirmed state. **Inputs/dependencies:** dialogue, exploration, combat, inventory, validation, saves. **P0 boundary:** only ending path, not daily/repeatable/event quests.\n+\n+### Party combat and balance\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** party member, enemy, ability, target, resource/status, encounter, result. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 tutorialises first battle; J2 gives clear turn feedback. Validate actor/action/target/resource/turn before mutation. Empty ability/no legal target/invalid command has controlled messaging; defeat follows checkpoint recovery. **Inputs/dependencies:** authored encounters/abilities/enemies; scenes, feedback, progression, rewards, saves. **P0 boundary:** no multiplayer/competitive features. Party size, formulae, count and balance targets require approval.\n+\n+### Inventory and equipment\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** item definition, stack, inventory, equipment slot, reward claim. **Rules/outcomes:** J2 supports readable inspection and legal use/equip. Empty inventory is instructional; invalid item/target/quantity changes nothing. **Inputs/dependencies:** item content, combat/quest rewards, UI/accessibility, saves. **P0 boundary:** no trade, crafting, market, or paid items. Capacity is undecided: avoid it or define unclaimed-reward recovery before adding it.\n+\n+### Persistence, offline recovery, and data lifecycle\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** index, manual save, checkpoint, schema, backup/candidate, deletion. **Rules/outcomes:** J1 demonstrates save; J3 covers resume, corruption, storage denial/quota, incompatible data, no-data, migration and deletion. Preserve prior confirmed state on failed write/migration/update and show recovery; selected-slot deletion is confirmed. Remote sync conflict requires explicit future policy, never silent choice. **Inputs/dependencies:** storage and content version; supports shell, combat, inventory, progression, PWA. **P0 boundary:** local offline-capable persistence; no account/sync.\n+\n+### Presentation, input, accessibility, and localisation\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** responsive layout, action/binding, focus, settings profile, caption cue, visual setting, locale bundle. Settings load \u2192 edit \u2192 apply \u2192 persist. **Rules/outcomes:** J1/J4 work with keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad where browser/device support permits; dialogue/inventory/quest/progression UI stays readable on phone/tablet/desktop. Captions accompany relevant feedback. Permission-denied/unsupported hardware must not trap play; provide alternate advertised input. **Inputs/dependencies:** every UI domain, original assets, locale content, platform APIs. **P0 boundary:** no target-exclusive rules; language set/exact settings are open.\n+\n+### Original content, assets, authoring, and delivery\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** source assets and gameplay definitions, validation report, versioned package: draft \u2192 reviewed \u2192 validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 active/retired. **Rules/outcomes:** delivers original warm hand-painted, readable content for the complete P0 campaign. Validation checks required strings, links, exits, encounters, IDs, and asset availability; invalid packages cannot activate. **Inputs/dependencies:** feeds gameplay/presentation and release. **P0 boundary:** no copied assets/content, UGC/mod loading, or seasonal cadence.\n+\n+### PWA/platform, release, quality, and operations\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** install status, service-worker/cache version, candidate, active/rollback package, test evidence, error boundary, diagnostic event. Cache stages \u2192 validates \u2192 activates; rollback restores known-good assets, never saves. **Rules/outcomes:** J4 is installable and offline after caching. Offline asset miss, interrupted refresh, update, storage denial, and browser-feature denial are visible/recoverable. QA covers gameplay, persistence/recovery, offline/update, responsive/input/accessibility, compatibility, and approved performance budgets. Crash UI offers restart/menu/recovery where safe. **Inputs/dependencies:** package/version contracts, persistence, shell, privacy policy. **P0 boundary:** no backend uptime, paid support, or live events; support matrix/budgets/provider/rollback process need approval.\n+\n+### Privacy, security, identity, connected services, and commerce boundary\n+\n+**Entities/lifecycle:** consent, diagnostic record, account, remote replica, report/moderation case, entitlement. Only minimal diagnostics are a required candidate; all others are dormant interfaces. **Rules/outcomes:** collection/transmission requires approved minimisation, consent, retention, access and deletion policy. Permission-denied/offline connected paths preserve local play; future conflict policy is explicit. Purchases need entitlement/refund/regional/outage behavior; multiplayer needs age/safety/reporting/moderation/operations ownership. **Inputs/dependencies:** approved vendor, legal, security, operations. **P0 boundary:** account/sync, multiplayer/safety, live service, purchases/entitlements, advanced analytics and monetisation do not ship until their contradiction is resolved.\n+\n+## Prioritised feature catalogue\n+\n+| Priority/feature | Outcome/journey | Slice | Dependencies |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| P0 F01 Shell/new/resume | Safely begin or return (J1/J3). | New, load, pause, recovery navigation. | Saves, content, rendering. |\n+| P0 F02 Exploration | Progress campaign (J1/J2). | One town, one dungeon, interactions. | Content, input, quests, combat. |\n+| P0 F03 Narrative/ending | Understand and finish story (J2). | Original dialogue and short ending. | Content, locale, progression. |\n+| P0 F04 Quests/onboarding | Learn and know next goal (J1/J2). | Tutorial, bounded quest chain/rewards. | Narrative, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F05 Turn combat | Complete encounters (J1/J2). | Authored combat and defeat recovery. | Content, progression, inventory. |\n+| P0 F06 Inventory/rewards | Understand/use rewards (J2). | Inspect, grant, legal use/equip. | Content, combat, saves. |\n+| P0 F07 Persistence | Resume without silent loss (J1/J3). | Local saves, checkpoints, validation, recovery, deletion. | Storage, content version. |\n+| P0 F08 Accessible responsive input/settings | Play/read with preferences (J1/J4). | Responsive UI, inputs, text/captions/visual settings. | UI domains, platform APIs. |\n+| P0 F09 Original content delivery | Coherent original campaign (J1/J2). | Validated original packages/assets. | Authoring, release. |\n+| P0 F10 PWA/offline/update | Install and continue safely (J3/J4). | Installability, offline assets/saves, safe cache update. | Persistence, release. |\n+| P0 F11 Error recovery/quality | Recover from failure (J3/J4). | Player recovery UI, approved minimal diagnostics, target testing. | Shell, privacy decisions. |\n+| Gate G01 Account/remote state | Optional continuity only if approved. | Not P0; local profile/save only. | Privacy/security, backend. |\n+| Gate G02 Multiplayer/safety/live ops | Social play only if re-authorised. | Not P0; single player only. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Gate G03 Purchases/entitlements | Commerce only if re-authorised. | Not P0; no paid content. | Identity, legal, operations. |\n+| Deferred D01 Events, UGC, advanced analytics/monetisation | Extend later. | Explicitly deferred. | Content pipeline, connected policy. |\n+\n+## First-release completeness and target parity\n+\n+P0 completes J1\u2013J4 without G01\u2013G03 or D01: it is a complete local campaign, not a demo waiting on account, multiplayer, payment, or live-service work. Those interfaces cannot alter P0 rules, save ownership, or access to the ending.\n+\n+| Capability | Responsive public web | PWA | Intentional difference |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Campaign, rules, content, saves, settings/recovery | Full shared core. | Full shared core. | None. |\n+| Input/responsive UI | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; phone/tablet/desktop. | Same browser-supported model/layouts. | Capability may limit gamepad; alternate input remains. |\n+| Offline | Play after required assets cache; local campaign needs no connection. | Same. | PWA adds install/app-shell cache state. |\n+| Update safety | Saves separate from assets. | Same. | PWA stages/activates cache visibly without save mutation. |\n+| Account/commerce/connected services | Not P0. | Not P0. | None until approval. |\n+\n+## Decisions carried forward\n+\n+Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.\n\ntokens used\n69,290\n", "adapter_log": "The codebase-memory architecture call was cancelled by the environment; scoped repository discovery was used for the non-code Markdown sources.", "test_log": "Whitespace check passed; scoped content-presence check passed.", "browser_log": "Not applicable: documentation-only domain modelling.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Every feature maps to a user outcome and journey.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The J1\u2013J4 journey table and P0 catalogue map each first-release feature to user outcomes and journey IDs."}, {"criterion": "Normal, empty, invalid, permission-denied, offline, conflict, recovery, and deletion paths are specified where relevant.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Journeys, lifecycles, persistence, presentation, PWA, and connected-boundary chapters cover these paths."}, {"criterion": "The first release provides one complete useful journey without deferred dependencies.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The completeness section defines a local campaign completing J1\u2013J4 without connected-service gates."}, {"criterion": "Cross-target capability parity and intentional target-specific differences are documented.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "The target-parity table documents shared web/PWA core and intentional PWA installation/cache differences."}, {"criterion": "Each domain chapter defines its entities,